Preprocessing
=============

Purpose
-------

Prepare raw RF recordings for machine learning by applying preprocessing
operations before dataset generation.

Current Pipeline
----------------

Raw IQ Signal
↓
Peak Normalization
↓
Window Generation (Upcoming)
↓
Dataset Split (Upcoming)
↓
Training Dataset

Normalization
-------------

The first preprocessing stage is peak normalization.

Each complex IQ recording is scaled by its maximum magnitude.

Formula

    IQ_normalized = IQ / max(abs(IQ))

This ensures every recording has a maximum amplitude of 1 while preserving
its relative amplitude and phase information.

Implementation
--------------

Function

    normalize(iq)

Input

* Complex IQ samples
* numpy.ndarray
* Shape: (N,)

Output

* Peak-normalized IQ samples
* numpy.ndarray
* Shape: (N,)
* dtype: complex64

Advantages
----------

* Stable numerical range
* Faster neural network convergence
* Preserves signal phase
* Preserves relative amplitude relationships

Testing
-------

Normalization verified on

* DJI Inspire 2
* DJI Mavic Pro
* Wi-Fi (30 Mbps)
* Wi-Fi (50 Mbps)
* LTE (30 Mbps)
* LTE (50 Mbps)
* 5G NR

Validation performed

* Output remains complex.
* Shape remains unchanged.
* Maximum magnitude equals 1.
* No NaN values produced.

Limitations
-----------

Normalization is applied independently to each recording.

No dataset-wide normalization is currently implemented.

